{
  "id": "2026-11-13-aiplatform-v1",
  "date": "2026-11-13",
  "api": "aiplatform.v1",
  "service": "Vertex AI",
  "title": "Vertex AI Agent Status Writable Again; Discovery Engine Scopes Added",
  "summary": "Vertex AI has reversed a recent update, making `Agent.status` and `AgentStatus.state` properties writable once more, restoring developer control. Additionally, many `operations.get` methods now support new Discovery Engine-related OAuth scopes, indicating deeper integration with Agentspace, Vertex AI Search, and NotebookLM Enterprise.",
  "details": "Great news for developers managing Vertex AI Agents: the `status` property of `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1Agent` and the `state` property within `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1AgentStatus` are no longer read-only. This change rolls back a recent restriction (from 2026-11-06), giving you back control to modify these critical agent lifecycle fields.\n\nIn parallel, a significant number of `operations.get` methods across various Vertex AI resources (including `customJobs`, `datasets`, `models`, `pipelineJobs`, and many more) have expanded their OAuth scope requirements. They now accept `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/discoveryengine.assist.readwrite` and `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/discoveryengine.serving.readwrite`. These new scopes enable broader interaction with Discovery Engine products such as Agentspace, Vertex AI Search, and NotebookLM Enterprise, paving the way for more integrated AI solutions.",
  "impact": "medium",
  "breaking": false,
  "interesting_score": 8,
  "tags": [
    "Vertex AI",
    "Agents",
    "IAM",
    "Discovery Engine",
    "Rollback"
  ],
